# civil-holidays v1
# jurisdiction: IT
# source: https://www.normattiva.it/uri-res/N2Ls?urn:nulla&legge=1949-05-27;260
#   (Legge 27 maggio 1949, n. 260 "Disposizioni in materia di ricorrenze
#   festive", as amended by L. 90/1954 and DPR 792/1985 — the statutory list of
#   Italian national "festività". Twelve civil festività: 1 Jan, Epifania 6 Jan,
#   Pasqua and Lunedì dell'Angelo (Easter-relative via computus), 25 Apr
#   (Liberazione), 1 May, 2 Jun (Repubblica), Ferragosto 15 Aug, Ognissanti
#   1 Nov, Immacolata 8 Dec, Natale 25 Dec, Santo Stefano 26 Dec. Note: the
#   "Giornata dell'Unità Nazionale e delle Forze Armate" (4 Nov, celebrated the
#   first Sunday of November) is a solemn commemoration, NOT a work-free civil
#   festività, so it is deliberately omitted (see the reference differential in
#   test_holidays_it.py). Local copy papers/holidays/it_holidays.md.
#   MUNICIPAL patron-saint days (giorno del Santo Patrono): each comune's patron
#   feast is a recognised local holiday (L. 260/1949 art. 2). We ship the patron
#   feast of the 20 regional capitals as municipal-category entries keyed to the
#   capital's ISO 3166-2 province code, independently verified against
#   papers/holidays/it_holidays.md and https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santi_patroni_cattolici_delle_città_capoluogo_di_provincia_italiane.
# --- Remaining province patron days (derived from vacanza/holidays 0.101, MIT) ---
#   The other 87 of vacanza's 107 ISO 3166-2 province subdivisions (their 114
#   count also lists 7 duplicate "city" rows for Andria/Barletta/Cesena/Forlì/
#   Pesaro/Trani/Urbino sharing the same holidays as their parent province code
#   BT/FC/PU — omitted here as non-ISO duplicates). Structure (which saint, which
#   date, fixed vs movable) was seeded from vacanza's holidays/countries/italy.py
#   rather than independently re-verified per comune against a gazette, per the
#   house rule that permits vacanza-derived data as long as it is flagged as
#   such. Cross-reference: https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santi_patroni_cattolici_delle_città_capoluogo_di_provincia_italiane.
#   Where an existing capital-province row's holiday differs from vacanza's for
#   the same code (e.g. IT-PG), the pre-existing independently-verified row is
#   kept as-is and vacanza's differing entry is not force-merged in.
# retrieved: 2026-07-21
# categories: public|regional|municipal|religious|school
# columns: kind | name | args | categories | subdiv | observed
#
